6525f"},"feedback_items":[{"id":"F1","text":"Priority shared change — add generic lesson-shortcut rivals to `lesson-census`\n\n**Symptom.** Correct per-grid labels can still form an unteachable\nthree-demonstration/one-query window when all demonstrations hide the decisive\noperation. The current selected-task census is clean only against its declared\nrivals; the two independent audit targets expose generic shortcuts that their\nlocal contracts missed.\n\n**Concrete evidence.** `checks/audit/ead22faa41ef/counterexample.json` shows a\nreplace-all-colors shortcut matching all three demonstrations and failing the\nquery. `checks/audit/0cb23f5660c9/counterexample.json` shows an identity-crop\nshortcut matching three rotation-symmetric demonstrations and failing the\nasymmetric query.\n\n**Suggested change.** Extend the shared `arcpuzzles lesson-census` path with a\nsmall deterministic generic rival bank and an optional blocking policy for\n“matches every demonstration, differs on query.” Useful first rivals include\nwhole-grid versus local replacement, no-op/identity, omitted transform, crop\nwithout rotation/reflection, all-instances versus selected-instance, and\nfirst/last-object-only. Report each rival as applicable, refuted, equivalent, or\nambiguous; run production order and requested query rotations separately. Start\nadvisory and retain exact counterexample lessons so false positives can be\ntriaged before promotion."},{"id":"F2","text":"provide a shared strict-call validator for generated task APIs\n\n**Symptom.** The issued selected generator inherited permissive `GenCtx` coercion.\nThe baseline detector produced 123 `strict-scalar` warnings, including accepted\nboolean seeds, numeric difficulties, and float/string integer overrides.\n\n**Concrete evidence.** `checks/before/result.json`,\n`checks/tdd-red-strict/result.json`, and\n`checks/valid-output-parity.json` show the defect and the task-local repair. The\nfinal defect-lint and battery are green.\n\n**Suggested change.** Add a reusable public-boundary helper or decorator in the\nshared generator runtime/scaffold that validates seed, sample index, difficulty,\nand declared override types before `GenCtx` conversion. Preserve `None` as the\nno-override sentinel and reject booleans explicitly. New generators should get\nthis by construction; legacy tasks can migrate independently rather than changing\n`GenCtx` globally."},{"id":"F3","text":"reject fixed-parent canonical paths when task tests are authored\n\n**Symptom.** Audit target `ead22faa41ef` has a task test that assumes a fixed\n`Path.parents[...]` depth. The portable task-test preflight therefore exits 2\nbefore test execution.\n\n**Concrete evidence.** The exact diagnostic is retained in\n`checks/audit/ead22faa41ef/task-tests/result.json`.\n\n**Suggested change.** Have the test scaffold or authoring linter reject fixed\nparent-depth guesses for canonical data and offer the supported replacement:\n`reviewer_support.find_root(__file__)`, `canonical_path`, and `canonical_pairs`.\nA small autofix for the common pattern would make old task suites portable.\n\nThe selected task-local validator, regression tests, notes, and parametric\nprototype are already included in this return. F1–F3 require shared-tool or\ncross-task decisions and are not mixed into the selected-task patch."}],"packet_id":"ee835cf31b5faa0498e135f699e5f09949b0bd6bf3b943d18a7a0a0152610e41","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"9c79cbe3eda497bf6b51e6c48b671f2b7d0e3d0f3fdd12f427c7a211bcf09963","instance_hash":"4db00e6f55180394fb70e39cf2148329109a34c23529759b730393cde0de8953","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"solve_kind":"blind_before_repair","source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished","task_id":"5a8d42591332"},"reviewer_solve